   ],
   "textLength": 265,
   "text": "Melanie Sumner: My name is Melanie Sumner and I am a software engineer\nspecializing in digital accessibility. I've been writing code for the web for\n25 years. My first career was… kind of a spy. I was an intelligence analyst in\nthe US Navy, and coding was my hobby.",
   "counts": {
    "links": 0,
    "images": 1,
    "headings": 0,
    "listItems": 0,
    "tableRows": 0,
    "controls": 0,
    "paragraphs": 2,
    "repeats": 1,
    "coverLinks": 0
   },
   "images": [
    {
     "kind": "img",
     "alt": "Melanie Sumner's headshot.",
     "width": 350,
     "height": 350
    }
   ],
   "linkTextRatio": 0,
   "geometry": {
    "top": 728,
    "height": 140,
    "widthFraction": 0.59,
    "leftFraction": 0.23,
    "pageFraction": 0.11,
    "aboveFold": true
   }
  },
  {
   "index": 13,
   "tag": "p×5",
   "landmarks": [
    "section",
    "section",
    "main",
    "article"
   ],
   "textLength": 1152,
   "text": "I didn't really like being a spy. I wasn't fond of death, it turns out. As most\npeople are not, when they have to be closer to it. I had to decide what I\nwanted to do next, and it was time to turn my hobby into my career. In the last\n10 years, I've really focused on software engineering in the accessibility\nspace, specifically.\nAlexandra: You don't often hear, \"Oh first I was a spy.\" No big deal. ",
   "counts": {
    "links": 1,
    "images": 0,
    "headings": 0,
    "listItems": 0,
    "tableRows": 0,
    "controls": 0,
    "paragraphs": 5,
    "repeats": 5,
    "coverLinks": 1
   },
   "linkTextRatio": 0.02,
