   "landmarks": [
    "section",
    "section",
    "main",
    "article"
   ],
   "textLength": 2267,
   "text": "As I learned more about the state and federal requirements and began reading\nthe W3C Accessibility spec, I thought, \"All of\nthis makes sense.\" Most of the web wasn't compliant, from what I could see. Of\ncourse, people have been working on web accessibility for as long as the web\nhas existed. Sometimes JavaScript engineers (in particular) are a little slow\non the uptake when it comes to digital acc",
